  "teach": "## Using cases\n\nLatin shows the job of a noun with **endings**, not word order alone.\n\n- *Puella terram spectat.* — The girl looks at the land. (*puella* nom. subject; *terram* acc. object)\n- *Aqua est in silvā.* — Water is in the forest. (*in* + ablative for place where)\n\n### sum (present), quick look\n\n| | sing. | plural |\n|--|----|----|\n| 1 | sum | sumus |\n| 2 | es | estis |\n| 3 | est | sunt |\n\n*Puella est in villā.* — The girl is in the country house.\n\n### Your job this lesson\n\nTranslate carefully. If you miss the standard, use **More practice** for extra items, or ask the tutor.",
